{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "control": "S"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 125, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a skip where edge 3 is empty creates a new input-to-output residual path, which gains much more than replacing an existing op."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing the input-to-output identity residual hurts more than removing a conv or pool on that edge."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the identity shortcut with a conv destroys the residual path, offsetting any capacity gain."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 1 already absent, removing edge 0 disconnects nodes 1 and 2 from the input, leaving only edge 3."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 0 already absent, removing edge 1 disconnects the intermediate nodes from the input."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a weak parameter-free pool with a conv gains far more than replacing skip or none."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Upgrading an avg_pool to a conv on the node 1 to node 2 edge adds substantial learnable capacity compared with replacing other ops."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "A residual on edge 3 protects the network from degradation when a conv is downgraded to pooling."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without a direct input-to-outp